{"admissible_as_evidence":true,"certificate_verdict":{"note":"SEALED 9 Aug: the per-class Gaussian margin certificate FAILS to predict the measured M116 crossing (KS1 fired: no crossing at any lambda; KS2 fired: predicted dense 0.9998 > sparse 0.0035 at n_max, measured 0.2153 > 0.1972). The model predicts sparse ~ chance at every data size and dense -> ~1.0, both contradicted by measurement. Per the registered fallback (v19 5.2), the certificate is CLOSED as a prediction tool and kept as an explanatory diagnostic only. Diagnostic content: (1) the spectral facts reproduce M121 (sparse captures 3.4x more label power, eff-rank 8 vs 30); (2) the failure mode is instructive: the Canatar per-class score variance makes dense's score noise vanish (its few captured modes are learned instantly), yet the MEASURED dense accuracy (0.1972) is far from the model's near-perfect prediction - the 345-channel argmax is far more sensitive than the population-spectrum Gaussian model captures, confirming M121's conclusion that the accuracy crossing is an argmax phenomenon no spectral MSE/margin proxy built from the Gram spectrum + label projections alone tracks.","registered_conclusion_licenses":"M123 fires under the registered gate; the firing is about the spectral prediction TOOL, not about the existence of learnable label power in the sparse span (11.8% vs 3.5%, reproduced)."},"config":{"gate":{"gap_direction_at_nmax":"predicted sparse accuracy(n_max) > dense accuracy(n_max) (matches M116's measured 0.2153 > 0.1972)","predicted_crossing":"smallest ladder P where predicted sparse accuracy(P) > dense accuracy(P); PASS if within a factor [1/3, 3] of the measured M116 crossing midpoint (41400)","registered_fallback":"if the margin certificate still fails to predict the crossing, the certificate is CLOSED as a prediction tool and kept as an explanatory diagnostic only (per v19 section 5.2)"},"milestone":"M123","numerics":{"eigh_backend":"numpy.linalg.eigh (CPU, M107 arithmetic convention)","gram_dtype":"float64","kappa_fixed_point_iters":200,"kappa_fixed_point_tol":1e-12,"seed":109,"torch_threads":16},"registered_before_any_accuracy":true,"registered_in":"analysis/RESEARCH_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN_v19.md section 5.2 (M123)","source":{"features":"reuses M116's sealed feature memmaps (data_cache_root()/v16/m116/f_train.npy 138000x12288 float32; dense_train.npy 138000x768 float32); no re-encoding, no training","m116_reference":"logs/results/v16/m116_scale/evidence.json (measured Q(n); sparse overtakes dense between n=27600 and n=55200)"},"theory":{"disclosure":"first-principles Gaussian margin approximation: (i) class-conditional modal means = train-class averages (exchangeability); (ii) E[b_rho^2] = 1 for standardised features (isotropic test-input covariance); (iii) joint score vector Gaussian. The covariance carries the P-dependence (E_rho -> 0 as P grows, so predicted accuracy rises); the mean carries the class-alignment structure (S/(vals+kappa)). The gate is the predicted CROSSING (shape-level), never absolute accuracy. Target power in kernel-null modes contributes ~0 to S and Sigma (a_rho ~ 0 there; no division by vals that explodes), reported as a per-class diagnostic, not gated.","eigenvalues":"eta_rho = eigenvalues of (1/M) F_std^T F_std, M = 138000 train rows, per-dim mean/unit-variance from train (the M116 RidgeAccumulator convention); kept modes as M121 (vals > max*1e-10)","formula":"Canatar-Bordelon-Pehlevan 2006.13198 modal machinery (as in M121) applied PER CLASS, then a Gaussian score-margin model. Modal objects from the full-M standardised Gram: vals_k (raw eigenvalues), a_rho,c = v_rho^T (F_std^T y_c) (345-dim label projections per mode), kappa(P) and E_rho(P) = (1/(1-gamma)) kappa^2/(kappa + P*eta)^2 from the M121 fixed point. Per ladder point P: S_cc'(P) = sum_rho a_rho,c a_rho,c' / (vals_k + kappa(P)); Sigma_cc'(P) = sum_rho E_rho(P) a_rho,c a_rho,c' / vals_k (Canatar's modal error applied per class and pairwise - the per-class learnable score VARIANCE, decaying as P grows). Score model for a class-c test point: f ~ N(mu^(c)(P), Sigma(P)) with mu^(c)_c'(P) = S_cc'(P) / n_c (class-conditional modal mean estimated by the train average, exchangeability). Predicted accuracy(P) = (1/C) sum_c P(f_c > max_{c'!=c} f_c'), Monte Carlo over the Gaussian.","ladder":[6900,13800,27600,55200,110400,138000],"lambda_grid":[0.1,1.0,10.0],"mc_seed":109,"n_mc_samples":10000,"ridge_mapping":"lambda = penalty = 1.0 (the program's closed-form ridge), kappa(P) self-consistently as in M121"},"title":"Classification-aware certificate: does a per-class score-margin model, built from the Gram spectrum and label projections alone, predict M116's measured accuracy crossing? (the M121 fix)"},"config_file":"m123_margin_certificate.json","gates":{"_smoke_skip":false,"kill_switch_1_crossing":{"factor_hi":3.0,"factor_lo":0.3333333333333333,"fired":true,"lambda":1.0,"measured_midpoint":41400.0,"predicted_crossing":null,"registered":"predicted crossing (sparse margin-accuracy > dense) within factor [1/3, 3] of the measured M116 crossing midpoint (41400)"},"kill_switch_2_gap_direction":{"fired":true,"measured_dense_acc_nmax":0.1971594202898551,"measured_reference_n":138000,"measured_sparse_acc_nmax":0.2152753623188406,"predicted_dense_nmax":0.9997901449275364,"predicted_sparse_nmax":0.003513043478260867,"registered":"predicted sparse margin-accuracy > dense at n_max (matches measured accuracy order 0.2153 > 0.1972)"},"lambda_grid_sensitivity":{"crossing_per_lambda":{"0.1":null,"1.0":null,"10.0":null}}},"margin_curves":{"dense":{"0.1":{"curve":{"110400":1.0,"13800":0.9997249275362319,"138000":1.0,"27600":0.9999947826086957,"55200":1.0,"6900":0.9975182608695652},"per_p":{"110400":{"kappa":0.10069867159518762,"margin_pct":{"25":0.01870984235828535,"5":0.018701478331347374,"50":0.018699119924419846,"75":0.01866856498887596,"95":0.018728899495213808},"mean_diag_ratio":1411350120.5177271,"predicted_accuracy":1.0,"sigma_trace":3.383445425055